cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the associated journal article and this archived repository."
type: software
title: "PVOS: Parallel Variation Operator Strategy research code and data"
abstract: >-
  Source code, configuration files, raw per-run results, and post-processing
  notebooks for the Parallel Variation Operator Strategy (PVOS), a fixed-budget
  operator-level multi-crossover ensemble for multi-objective evolutionary
  optimization. Includes PVOS-2C and PVOS-4C implementations, four adaptive
  operator-selection baselines (Borg, HNSGA, EnXEA, OVEA) under a common
  four-operator pool, host-transfer integrations with NSGA-II, SPEA2, NSGA-III,
  and AGE-MOEA2, the styrene monomer reactor case study (single-bed,
  steam-injected, double-bed), the ordered 30-seed list, configuration files,
  raw per-run CSVs, crossover-survival logs, and notebooks that reproduce all
  reported tables and figures.

